Print """
The default variable name is $record"""
Select *
From 1 /* As $record */
For Template

Print """
With various options"""
Select * From 1 For Record Template
Select * From 1 For Batch Template
Select * From 1 For Batch Template Include Headers
Select * From 1 For Batch Template Exclude Headers

Print """
Ordinals are treated as a single entry array"""
Select *
From "A"
For Batch Template

Print """
Arrays can contain mixed types
but including dictionaries change this behavior"""
Select *
From [ True, False, None, Inf, vgr.version ] As Data
For Batch Template

Print """
Not that the From ... As name has to be a variable name.
It is not a label."""
Select *
From [ True, False ] As "A_Boolean" /* variable name, not a label */
For Batch Template

Print """
The * can be used multiple times, as can any column.
Select will give the columns unique labels if there are
collisions."""
Select
    *, *
From [ True, False ]
For Batch Template

Print """
Select maintains a variable reflecting the current
row number. $rec-index starts at zero."""
Select
    $rec-index, *
From [ "A", "B", "C" ] As Character
For Batch Template

Print """
$rec-index reflects the input sequence, not the output"""
Select
    $rec-index, *
From [ "A", "B", "C" ] As Character
Where Character >= "B"
For Batch Template

Define Function row_number():
    Set rc To counter
    Add 1 To counter
    Return rc
End-Function

Print """
You can use a function to number output rows.
Also, you can use any variable, constant, or expression
as a column value."""
Set counter To 1
Select
    @row_number() As "Output Row",
    $rec-index As "Input Row",
    *
From [ "A", "B", "C", "D" ] As Character
Where Character Is Not In ["B", "D"]
For Batch Template

Print """
You can directly use the variable in an expression
instead of using "*".
Note that the labels for columns can be unquoted but
only if they do not collide with a variable in use."""
Select
    Character.Repr() As Value, /* can be quoted or not */
    Character.Upper().Repr() As "Upper",
    Character.Lower().Repr() As "Lower"
From [ "A", "b", "c", "D" ] As Character
Where Character.Upper() Is Not In ["B", "D"]
For Batch Template

Print """
There is a special case for using a single dictionary:
Select iterates over the keys and values in the dictionary
just like "For-Each"
Note: the full names of the properties are "$record.key" and "$record.value"
  The Select automatically add the correct prefix as long as the
  name does not collide with a variable that is alread set."""
Select
    key, value
From {"first_name":"Bailey","last_name":"Cisco","email":"bciscoa@deviantart.com","position":"Director of Sales","age":47}
For Batch Template

Print """
Select is typically used from a list of data structured as a list of dictionaries"""
Set filename To vgr.source.FirstItem().DirectoryName() + "/people.json"
Load people From File filename

Select *
From people
Limit 5 /* limits the number of rows output */
For Batch Template
# Also available:
# Limit <value> Offset <value> : skip of the first N rows
# Fetch First <value> Rows Only : Limit alias, but SQL compatible

Print """
Use column labels and expressions to format the data."""
Select
    RightJustify(age.DefaultTo(Space), 3) As "age".Capitalize(), /* labels are expressions */
    last_name.DefaultTo(Space) As "Last Name",
    first_name.DefaultTo(Space) As "First Name",
    position.DefaultTo(Space) As "Position",
    email.DefaultTo(Space) As "Email"
From people As person
Limit 5
For Batch Template

Print """
Select can read directly from a file."""
Select
    RightJustify($rec-index + 1, 3) As "Row",
    RightJustify(age.DefaultTo(Space), 3) As "age".Capitalize(), /* labels are expressions */
    last_name.DefaultTo(Space) As "Last Name",
    first_name.DefaultTo(Space) As "First Name",
    email.DefaultTo(Space) As "Email"
From File filename
    Type is JSON Encoding Is "UTF-8" /* optional values */
Where (age Is None Or first_name Is None) And email Is Not None
Limit 5
For Batch Template

Print """
Data can be written in multiple formats.

JSON-"""
Select *
From File filename
Where (age Is None Or first_name Is None) And email Is Not None
Limit 5
For JSON
    Compact, Sort Keys, Exclude Nulls

Print """
CSV-"""

Select *
From File filename
Where (age Is None Or first_name Is None) And email Is Not None
Limit 5
For CSV
    Exclude Headers,
    Include Headers,         // last one wins
    Quote Char Is Quote,     // use Char or Character
    Quoting Style Is All,    // All, None, Minimal, NonNumeric
    Line Terminator Is Newline,
    Escape Character Is Backslash,
    Delimiter Is Comma

Print """
Markdown-"""
Select *
From File filename
Where (age Is None Or first_name Is None) And email Is Not None
Limit 5
For Markdown
    Exclude Headers Is False,  // optional expression
    Include Headers Is True    // these are equivalent

Print """
Text-"""
Select *
From File filename
Where (age Is None Or first_name Is None) And email Is Not None
Limit 5
For Text
    Include Headers,
    Exclude Nulls,
    Field Separator Is "!!",
    Header Separator Is "::",
    Record Separator Is "<" + Newline

Print """
The result of Select can be sent to a specific destination
using the Into clause.

To stdout (the default)-"""
Select *
From File filename
Limit 5
For CSV
Into Output /* this is the default */

Print """
To stderr-"""
Select *
From File filename
Limit 5
For CSV
Into Error

Print """
To a file-"""
Set output_file To "out.data"
Select *
From File filename
Limit 5
For CSV
Into File output_file Encoding Is "ASCII" /* encoding is optional */
Load data_in From File output_file Type Is Text /* but we could read as CSV if we wanted */
Printf "{}", data_in
Assert RemoveFile(output_file).FirstItem()
Unset data_in

Print """
To a variable (as text)-"""
Select *
From File filename
Limit 5
For CSV Quoting Style Minimal, Exclude Header
Into select_out
Printf "{}", select_out
Unset select_out
